            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0511" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/637: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-18T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>318. Your 816, August 17, 10 p.m. Action outlined in your telegram of August 17,
                    10 p.m., to Consulate at Shanghai is approved <pb facs="0512" n="404"
                        xml:id="pg404"/> by the Department. Department agrees with you that Consul
                    should not intervene in question of legal remedies.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
